{"agent":"bg102","data":{"by":"bg102","evidence":{"diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"note":"CONFIRMED: baseline_red.on_base builds todo as [i for i in ids if i not in known or (known.get(i) and (i not in cached_sigs or len(cached_sigs[i]) == LINE_CHARS))], so any cached base signature exactly LINE_CHARS long is re-measured on EVERY gate run. A genuinely-whole reason of exactly 240 chars is indistinguishable from a legacy cut-to-240 entry, so it is redundantly re-run (the bug). Verified by reading the code at ddflow/services/gates/baseline_red.py:100-105 and flakes.LINE_CHARS=240; ruby_demo: cache_store(cut==240) then on_base -> todo non-empty.","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/services/gates/__init__.py":"100644 a2dfdc3a30a134758037d74027f64bf0ea359afe","ddflow/services/gates/baseline.py":"100644 ce658d26b28b07d13f91a2121cba0fb10a022cfe","ddflow/services/gates/baseline_red.py":"100644 973f017da88572e07835e49e350d577c97a8838d","tests/test_gate_baseline_red.py":"100644 2cc457cf172e09be584473cc56cb5cabd66a4c93"},"tree_sha":"6df5a765f960+clean"},"gate":"research","reason":""},"id":"e2f8790ba8031595123634023","kind":"gate.passed","lamport":158047,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B60e9e09308","ts":"2026-11-09T00:19:12.596679Z"}
